  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": "Many languages use different words for a mother's brother and a father's brother, or for an uncle by birth and an uncle by marriage. English **uncle** covers all of these relatives.",
    "grammar": null,
    "culture": "In some cultures children call any older man *uncle* to show respect. In English-speaking countries this is less common and usually means a close family friend.",
